** AUTHORED TEMPLATE — gain_stage/dc_op: self-biased DC operating point + supply current.
** An inverting gain stage has a narrow high-gain input window that moves with PDK/corner, so a
** fixed input bias is useless: a 1 TH feedback inductor DC-shorts vout back to vin instead
** (the amplifier-class bias-wrap trick), self-biasing the stage at its trip point vin = vout.
** Reports that trip voltage (v_trip) and the supply current at the ACTIVE operating point.
** Class port convention: vdd vout vin ibias vss; `ibias` is SINK-referenced (the DUT holds a
** PMOS-side diode at ibias, the bench pulls IBIAS out of it to vss).
